{"id":"liver","cards":[{"id":"liver122fa0c2","l":1,"f":"<b>Portal venous inflow</b> — Structure?","b":"<b>Portal vein</b>","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liver5d443812","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic arterial inflow</b> — Structure?","b":"<b>Hepatic artery</b>","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liverd883b535","l":1,"f":"<b>Venous outflow</b> — Structure?","b":"<b>Hepatic vein</b>","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liver1700c952","l":1,"f":"<b>Biliary drainage</b> — Structure?","b":"<b>Bile duct</b>","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liverc58fbefc","l":2,"f":"Structure <b>not</b> in the portal triad","b":"<b>hepatic vein</b> (triad = portal vein, hepatic artery, bile duct)","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liver857318ff","l":1,"f":"<b>Healthy liver</b> — Tolerance of Resection?","b":"Can tolerate <b>major resection (~70%)</b>","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liver287b37d7","l":1,"f":"<b>Cirrhotic/injured liver</b> — Tolerance of Resection?","b":"May look large yet have <b>very poor reserve</b> → even small resection can cause <b>post-hepatectomy liver failure</b>","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liver73974fc9","l":1,"f":"<b>Decompensated cirrhosis</b> — Tolerance of Resection?","b":"<b>Generally not suitable</b> for hepatic resection","c":"Liver Surgical Anatomy"},{"id":"liver6e1a605b","l":1,"f":"<b>Hemangioma</b> — Nature?","b":"<b>Most common</b> benign tumor (~5%); vascular/blood-filled","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liverc67d27ac","l":1,"f":"<b>FNH</b> — Nature?","b":"<b>Hyperplasia</b> of otherwise normal hepatocytes","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver01ec7540","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic Adenoma</b> — Nature?","b":"<b>Premalignant</b>; <b>OCP/hormone</b>- associated","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liverb39e9a1f","l":1,"f":"<b>Hemangioma</b> — Key imaging?","b":"<b>Peripheral → centripetal fill-in</b>; T2 very bright","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver308b5948","l":1,"f":"<b>FNH</b> — Key imaging?","b":"<b>Central scar</b> with radiating spokes (\"orange segments\")","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liverecd5f37f","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic Adenoma</b> — Key imaging?","b":"May be hard to distinguish from <b>early</b> <b>HCC</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver965fdd71","l":1,"f":"<b>Hemangioma</b> — Malignant potential?","b":"None","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver7a1b92d8","l":1,"f":"<b>FNH</b> — Malignant potential?","b":"<b>None</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver451f634d","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic Adenoma</b> — Malignant potential?","b":"<b>→ HCC</b>; also <b>rupture/hemorrhage</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liverf423488f","l":1,"f":"<b>Hemangioma</b> — Biopsy?","b":"<b>Avoid</b> — bleeding, non-diagnostic","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver4f42b1b1","l":1,"f":"<b>FNH</b> — Biopsy?","b":"Unnecessary — shows normal liver","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liverc384f486","l":1,"f":"<b>Hemangioma</b> — Management Hemangioma?","b":"Usually <b>observe</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver3ef51da5","l":1,"f":"<b>FNH</b> — Management Hemangioma?","b":"Usually <b>no treatment</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver6a5e251c","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic Adenoma</b> — Management Hemangioma?","b":"<b>Stop OCP</b> → observe ≤1 yr → persistent → <b>surgery</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"livercccca5e5","l":1,"f":"<b>Non-contrast</b> — Contrast Location?","b":"No contrast in aorta","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver60d3cb3d","l":1,"f":"<b>Arterial</b> — Contrast Location?","b":"Predominantly in <b>aorta/arterial system</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"livercfd290f4","l":1,"f":"<b>Portal venous</b> — Contrast Location?","b":"Portal system/liver enhances after blood returns from <b>bowel/spleen</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver176ccb6f","l":1,"f":"<b>Delayed</b> — Contrast Location?","b":"Contrast drains through <b>hepatic veins</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liverafae3393","l":2,"f":"Peripheral nodular enhancement with <b>centripetal fill-in</b>","b":"<b>haemangioma</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver4835a05e","l":2,"f":"Hypervascular lesion with a <b>central stellate scar</b> → <b>FNH</b> ; incidental 3-cm FNH","b":"<b>no treatment needed</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver8438c152","l":2,"f":"OCP user, incidental <b>arterially enhancing</b> mass → <b>stop OCPs, repeat imaging in 6 months</b> ; adenoma <b>not regressing 6 months after stopping OCP</b>","b":"<b>surgical resection</b>","c":"Benign Liver Masses"},{"id":"liver8c244b40","l":2,"f":"Cyst that can look like a <b>solid mass</b> on CT","b":"<b>hydatid cyst</b> (degenerated/calcified type)","c":"Liver Cysts"},{"id":"liverf71da124","l":2,"f":"Most serious complication of hepatic <b>hydatid</b> disease","b":"<b>anaphylaxis</b> (rupture/spillage)","c":"Liver Cysts"},{"id":"liver094258b3","l":2,"f":"<b>Amoebic</b> liver abscess (positive E. histolytica serology)","b":"initial <b>antiamoebic drugs (metronidazole)</b>","c":"Liver Cysts"},{"id":"livercd0e1846","l":2,"f":"Egyptian man with <b>bilharziasis</b>","b":"<b>HCC</b> risk (schistosomiasis + HCV co-infection)","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"livera85f306b","l":2,"f":"Paraneoplastic syndromes of HCC — all except","b":"keyed <b>hyperglycaemia</b> (HCC causes hypoglycaemia, hypercalcaemia, hypercholesterolaemia, erythrocytosis)","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liver00de3943","l":2,"f":"Weakest association with HCC (smoker on HRT with HBV + HCV) → <b>OCP/hormones</b> ; all predispose except","b":"keyed <b>smoking</b> (least risk; hepatitis A causes no chronic disease)","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liver9b16e923","l":2,"f":"HBV cirrhosis, jaundice and weight loss, <b>hypervascular mass</b>","b":"confirm with <b>α-fetoprotein</b>","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liverbd783667","l":1,"f":"<b>Local</b> — Details?","b":"<b>Satellite lesions</b> around the primary mass","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liverbd95b31e","l":1,"f":"<b>Vascular</b> — Details?","b":"<b>Venous/tumor thrombus</b>","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liver4e382a8a","l":1,"f":"<b>Lung</b> — Details?","b":"Hepatic veins → IVC → heart → <b>lungs</b>","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liver2ce0df7c","l":1,"f":"<b>Bone</b> — Details?","b":"<b>Vertebral</b> metastases → spinal symptoms/compression","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liver5aa359d8","l":1,"f":"<b>Brain</b> — Details?","b":"Also discussed","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liverda8d9ac9","l":2,"f":"\"All are liver cysts except\"","b":"<b>metastasis</b> (from colon cancer is solid)","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liverf49ef73b","l":2,"f":"Pyogenic liver abscess with <b>Streptococcus faecalis</b> (gut organism)","b":"spread via the <b>portal route</b>","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liveracb5eb79","l":1,"f":"<b>General oncology</b> — Biopsy??","b":"Tissue usually required — <b>\"no tissue, no issue\"</b>","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liverb6fab901","l":1,"f":"<b>Cirrhotic + classic enhancement + washout</b> — Biopsy??","b":"<b>Not required</b> — radiological diagnosis","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liverdec2d34a","l":1,"f":"<b>Non-cirrhotic or atypical imaging</b> — Biopsy??","b":"<b>Required</b>","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"livera841dcbf","l":2,"f":"HCV cirrhosis, 2-cm lesion with <b>early arterial enhancement and early washout</b>","b":"<b>HCC</b>","c":"Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)"},{"id":"liverdf274887","l":2,"f":"4-cm HCC with <b>Child B</b> cirrhosis","b":"<b>liver transplant</b>","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver9a1f652c","l":1,"f":"<b>Child A</b> — Score?","b":"<b>5–6</b>","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver99602e07","l":1,"f":"<b>Child A</b> — Lecture Treatment Framing?","b":"<b>Preserved function</b> → potentially suitable for definitive local/<b>resection</b> therapy","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver575a8904","l":1,"f":"<b>Child B</b> — Score?","b":"<b>7–9</b>","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liverbfad4c97","l":1,"f":"<b>Child B</b> — Lecture Treatment Framing?","b":"Especially 7–8 → consider <b>locoregional therapy</b>; 9 relatively advanced","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver007e8276","l":1,"f":"<b>Child C</b> — Score?","b":"<b>10–15</b>","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"livera7738f32","l":1,"f":"<b>Child C</b> — Lecture Treatment Framing?","b":"<b>Severe decompensation</b> → invasive/resection/locoregional treatment generally <b>poorly tolerated</b>","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liverde22f21f","l":1,"f":"<b>Technique RFA</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Needle into tumor → <b>heat</b> → protein denaturation/coagulative destruction","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver075d36f1","l":1,"f":"<b>Technique RFA</b> — Best Use?","b":"<b>Small lesions ≤3 cm</b>; high-risk/elderly patients. A <b>4 cm</b> lesion may exceed one standard zone → overlapping needles","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liverdbcaab28","l":1,"f":"<b>Cryotherapy</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>Extreme cold</b> (liquid nitrogen) → protein denaturation/cell destruction","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liverdd93efe4","l":1,"f":"<b>Cryotherapy</b> — Best Use?","b":"Both extreme heat and cold denature proteins","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liverb101a90e","l":1,"f":"<b>Ethanol injection</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>Absolute alcohol (~99%)</b> into tumor","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver8bff3bd5","l":1,"f":"<b>Ethanol injection</b> — Best Use?","b":"Older technique, before modern RFA/TACE","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver60c5ac63","l":1,"f":"<b>TACE</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>Super-selective</b> arterial catheterization → <b>chemotherapy</b> → <b>embolization</b> (retains drug, cuts arterial supply)","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liverc15d7cb3","l":1,"f":"<b>TACE</b> — Best Use?","b":"<b>Larger lesions</b> (e.g. <b>~12 cm → TACE, not RFA</b>); <b>bridging</b> to transplant","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver5eaa6ca5","l":1,"f":"<b>Radioembolization</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Intra-arterial radioactive particles → radiation <b>from within the</b> <b>lesion</b> <b>Assessing Response After Embolization/Ablation</b>","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liver54b0afc1","l":1,"f":"<b>Radioembolization</b> — Best Use?","b":"Larger tumors","c":"HCC Treatment"},{"id":"liverb30fab3f","l":1,"f":"<b>Hemangioma</b> — Gross Appearance?","b":"Cut surface resembles a <b>sponge/vascular spaces</b>","c":"Gross Appearance of Liver Tumors"},{"id":"liver293f4be4","l":1,"f":"<b>Tumor HCC</b> — Gross Appearance?","b":"Relatively <b>soft</b>; can undergo necrosis and <b>rupture/bleed</b>","c":"Gross Appearance of Liver Tumors"},{"id":"liverec0daf9a","l":1,"f":"<b>Cholangiocarcinoma</b> — Gross Appearance?","b":"Classically <b>very hard/solid</b>; <b>capsular retraction</b>","c":"Gross Appearance of Liver Tumors"}]}